  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Knowledge Management Project Phase VII</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project, which will build upon the previous six phases, seeks to promote coordination, information sharing, and knowledge management among the regional migration capacity building programs (RMPs) and other global and multiregional projects funded by the United States Department of State Bureau of Population, Refugees and Migration&apos;s Office of International Migration (PRM); and promote innovative approaches to capacity building that are evidence-based. The project coordinates the capture and sharing of knowledge developed in RMP projects, both within and between the three RMPs, and within IOM more broadly. It also provides donor liaison and coordination support between IOM (all relevant missions) and PRM to ensure adequate coordination, communications, and project support.</narrative>
  </description>
